# living-docs (standing)

Follow the installed **living-docs** skill. Default: fix the code, write no doc.

Write a lesson only when the same class was corrected before (or the user asks), and put it where it fires: architecture → types → linter → test → review/verify checklist step → prose last. If a prose rule for the class already exists and the mistake happened anyway, move it up a level or delete it — don't reword or extend it. Reply in one line: what changed, or "no doc — <reason>".
